Gradient Descent and SGD on Make Moons Dataset
Aim

To implement and compare Batch Gradient Descent and Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD) for training a neural network from scratch using NumPy.

Dataset Used

The Make Moons dataset from sklearn.datasets is used.

400 samples

2 input features

Binary classification

Noise = 0.20

The features are standardized before training.

Methods Used

Batch Gradient Descent: Uses the entire dataset for one weight update per epoch.

Mini-Batch SGD: Uses batches of 16 samples, resulting in multiple updates per epoch.

Results

Both methods are used to train the same neural network architecture. The final training accuracy for Batch Gradient Descent and SGD is displayed after 200 epochs.

Example output:

Batch GD accuracy: XX.XX
SGD accuracy: XX.XX


The exact accuracy may vary depending on the training process.

